The five longest rivers and their source elevations are: 
1. Nile: Rukarara tributary source at ~2,539 m; 
2. Amazon: Mantaro River headwaters at ~5,674 m (or traditional Nevado Mismi at ~5,597 m); 
3. Yangtze: Jari Hill (Dam Qu) at ~5,170 m (or traditional Geladandong at ~5,342–5,446 m); 
4. Mississippi-Missouri-Jefferson: Brower's Spring at ~2,338 m; 
5. Yenisey-Angara-Selenga: Ider River headwaters at ~3,900–3,950 m.
